 "answer": "## Solution\n\nSince 233 is prime, by Fermat's Little Theorem: 71^232 \u2261 1 (mod 233).\n\nI'll compute 71^390 mod 233 directly using repeated squaring, since 390 = 256+128+4+2 (binary: 110000110).\n\n**Compute powers of 71 mod 233 by squaring:**\n\n- 71\u00b9 = 71\n- 71\u00b2 = 71\u00b771 = 5041 \u2261 5041 \u2212 21\u00b7233 = 5041 \u2212 4893 = **148**\n- 71\u2074 = 148\u00b2 = 21904 \u2261 21904 \u2212 94\u00b7233 = 21904 \u2212 21902 = **2**\n- 71\u2078 = 2\u00b2 = **4**\n- 71\u00b9\u2076 = 4\u00b2 = **16**\n- 71\u00b3\u00b2 = 16\u00b2 = 256 \u2261 **23**\n- 71\u2076\u2074 = 23\u00b2 = 529 \u2261 529 \u2212 2\u00b7233 = **63**\n- 71\u00b9\u00b2\u2078 = 63\u00b2 = 3969 \u2261 3969 \u2212 17\u00b7233 = 3969 \u2212 3961 = **8**\n- 71\u00b2\u2075\u2076 = 8\u00b2 = **64**\n\n**Combine for exponent 390 = 256+128+4+2:**\n\n71^390 \u2261 71^256 \u00b7 71^128 \u00b7 71^4 \u00b7 71^2 (mod 233)\n= 64 \u00b7 8 \u00b7 2 \u00b7 148 (mod 233)\n\nStep by step:\n- 64\u00b78 = 512 \u2261 512 \u2212 466 = 46\n- 46\u00b72 = 92\n- 92\u00b7148 = 13616 \u2261 13616 \u2212 58\u00b7233 = 13616 \u2212 13514 = **102**\n\n**Verification check:** All intermediate reductions confirmed above.\n\nFINAL: 102"
